# The repository's own About box, in version control.
#
# GitHub's description, website and topics are otherwise a text field somebody
# typed once and nobody can review. `scripts/repo.sh apply` writes this file to
# the repository, `scripts/repo.sh check` fails when the two have drifted — and
# CI runs the check, so the About box is as reviewable as the README.
#
# POSIX sh: this file is sourced. Keep it to these three assignments.

DESCRIPTION="Read-only audit of a MariaDB/MySQL Galera cluster: the states its own wsrep_* metrics cannot show you — a system table drifted between nodes, one name covering two clusters, a proxy that disagrees, a gcache too small for the write rate. One static Go binary, SHOW and SELECT only."

HOMEPAGE="https://allan-nava.github.io/galera-doctor/"

# Max 20, lowercase, digits and hyphens only.
TOPICS="galera galera-cluster mariadb mysql proxysql wsrep replication split-brain database-tools dba sre devops observability audit read-only cli golang go"
